{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775348424-aikZL62cDJc9t8e7N8jU","role":"assistant","created":1775348431,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to extract the securities that have maturity dates in 1982. Looking at the table structure:\n- The first columns are: Date of final maturity | Description | Issue date | Total | Held by U.S. Govt accounts | All other investors\n- The second set of columns (after the first set of data) show 1988, 1989, etc.\n\nLet me parse the data more carefully. The table has rows for each year heading (1982, 1983, etc.) and the securities under each year.\n\nLooking at the 1982 section (the first section in the table):\n- Mar. 31: 2853, 4072\n- Apr. 30: *, 4573 (one is *)\n- May 15: 2747, 2613, 3556\n- June 30: 4284, 2594\n- July 31: 5215, 5337\n- Aug. 15: 2918, 3587\n- Aug. 31: 5127\n- Sept. 30: 2501, 5120\n- Oct. 1: 4823\n- Nov. 15: 2902, 2737\n- Nov. 30: 4966\n- Dec. 31: 4955, 3205\n\nWait, the table is a bit complex. It shows securities in chronological order. The first column block shows dates and amounts from 1982, and when we reach the next year (1983), it switches to the next column block.\n\nActually looking more carefully:\n- First header row: \"1982\" under the first set of columns\n- Then the actual securities for 1982 are listed\n- Then \"1983\" appears as a header for the next set\n- And so on\n\nThe table has:\n| Date of final maturity | Description | Issue date | Total | Held by U.S. Govt | All other investors | Date of final maturity.1 | Description.1 | Issue date.1 | Total.1 | ...\n\n\nI see two parallel columns of data - one for 1982 and another for 1988-1990. The first column block contains securities maturing in 1982, while the second shows securities from later years like 1988, 1989, and 1990. The Total column appears in the 4th position, so I need to isolate the rows specifically marked for 1982 and extract only those Total values.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_b7fc858efd784